Based on the dbt documentation, here's how to configure Claude Code to use dbt MCP:

## Configuration File Location

The configuration file should be named **`.mcp.json`** and placed at the **root of your project** (the repository root for your workspace).

**Source:** [integrate-mcp-claude.md](https://docs.getdbt.com/docs/dbt-ai/integrate-mcp-claude)

## Configuration Steps

### For Remote dbt MCP Server

1. Create or open `.mcp.json` at your project root
2. Get your MCP URL from the dbt Platform under **Account settings** → **Access URLs** → **MCP Endpoint URL**
3. Add the `dbt` entry using your authentication method:

**OAuth (if available for your account):**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "dbt": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://YOUR_DBT_HOST_URL/api/ai/v1/mcp/"
    }
  }
}
```

**Token-based:**
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "dbt": {
      "type": "http",
      "url": "https://YOUR_DBT_HOST_URL/api/ai/v1/mcp/",
      "headers": {
        "Authorization": "Token YOUR_DBT_ACCESS_TOKEN",
        "x-dbt-prod-environment-id": "DBT_PROD_ENV_ID",
        "x-dbt-user-id": "DBT_USER_ID",
        "x-dbt-dev-environment-id": "DBT_DEV_ENV_ID"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

4. Save the file. Claude Code picks up the configuration on startup.

### For Self-Hosted dbt MCP Server

You'll need to follow [Set up self-hosted MCP](/docs/dbt-ai/setup-local-mcp) to choose your authentication pattern, then add the appropriate configuration to `.mcp.json`.

## Important Note

The dbt documentation recommends committing `.mcp.json` to your repository so the setup is project-scoped and easier to share with your team, rather than using the user-level `claude mcp add` command which writes to `~/.claude.json`.

**Source:** [integrate-mcp-claude.md](https://docs.getdbt.com/docs/dbt-ai/integrate-mcp-claude)

